{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: extend the publication self-succession repair with fail-closed recovery of the retirement phase. Exact-head inspection found that a recovered already-visible successor can be settled without attempting its predecessor retirement, and a submitted supersession is recorded without verifying the fold decision.","body":{"branch":"request/notes-decisions-part-two-current","conditions":"Model assertion acceptance and required own-author predecessor retirement as separately durable, verified outbox phases. If reconciliation finds the successor assert already visible, it must still submit or resume and verify the required retirement. A retirement is complete only after the queried exact supersede event is visible and effective in the verified resident projection. Do not remove the batch or advance the repository publication frontier until all required own-author retirements are effective. Preserve bounded retry/abandonment rules without presenting a partial succession as published. Add a recovery test that begins with a visible successor assert and an unsuperseded own-author predecessor, reruns publication, and proves retirement becomes effective before frontier advance; add refusal coverage for an ineffective retirement decision. Implement and report this together with parent repair ef8100a1.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}